            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0781" n="649" xml:id="pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7748: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-15T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 15—3: 50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>481. My 472, October 12, 5 p.m. Following from American consul general, Hankow:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 14, 3 p.m. French gunboat <hi rendition="#italic">Alerte</hi>
                            fired upon yesterday near Wusüeh, killing one sailor, seriously injuring
                            another. <hi rendition="#italic">Alerte</hi> fired upon again below
                            Hankow this morning but no casualties. Fire returned both times.</p>
                        <p>Conditions at Wuchang continue to improve. Shops are opening and food
                            supplies ample. About 400 bodies inside and outside walls in crude
                            coffins now awaiting burial. All Northern troops evacuated.</p>
                        <p>No change in the situation at Kiukiang.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
